[36m(main_task pid=3614448)[0m 🤖 Response: The Great Depression led to the over-harvesting of trees and over-cutting of forests. Multiple air attacks on old growth forests were often carried out in Oregon, Washington, and California. In the three states of Oregon, Washington, and California, forests are reported to have been clear-cut in 1941. By 1941, the Oregon economy had ceased to be based on grazing and logging. The Clear-cutting method for most of the continental us left us with degraded land, barren hills, and eroded lands. It is a consequence of what was called commercial forestry. This practice is often seen as an outdated one. While it was a logical method in the days of the stream reclamation, it was found to be an erasing of the natural habitat of wildlife. Consequently, the public interest has played a role in the conservation of the forests in all states. However, Forest conservation is a modern policy and, with that, concerns arise. Thus, the time has come for widespread conservation of all natural forests.
