[36m(main_task pid=3614448)[0m 🤖 Response: The Kingdom of the Netherlands was invaded by Germany on May 10, 1940. The Battle of the Netherlands involved a four-day period, from May 10 to May 14, 1940, during which the conflict between the British Empire and Axis power escalated into fighting between German forces and the troops of the Kingdom of the Netherlands and Australia. Prior to May 10, 1940, only Canadian troops had been engaged in combat, in an amphibious operation known as Operation Ruby, which succeeded in reaching the Dutch East Indies to reinforce Allied forces against Japanese invasion. The British Expeditionary Force then formed a separate command, General Bernard Montgomery, and led it as the commander in chief of Operation Market Garden, a successful joint military operation where German forces were captured in the Netherlands. The Canadian troops were withdrawn from the eastern Dutch port of Paramaribo to return to the UK.
